  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): A 2-for-1 stock split doubles shares to 200,000 and halves par to $1 with no journal entry -- only a memo notation. A 100% stock dividend (large dividend per ASC 505-20-25-4, exceeding 20-25%) requires debiting retained earnings $200,000 and crediting common stock at par. The split leaves all equity components unchanged while the dividend shifts $200,000 from retained earnings to common stock.
Wrong (A): The alternatives do not produce identical effects -- the stock dividend requires a retained earnings transfer while the split does not.
Wrong (C): This reverses the treatment -- the split requires no retained earnings transfer, while the dividend does.
