  choices = $EXPL$["Both old and new debt are reported as liabilities, and the $400,000 difference is expensed immediately in the current period","The old debt is removed, the new debt is reported, and the $400,000 is recognized as interest expense in the current period","The old debt is removed, the new debt is reported, and the $400,000 is a deferred outflow amortized over the shorter remaining life","The old debt remains on the statement of net position until the escrow trust formally retires it at maturity"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB 86 and GASB 65 paragraph 7, when debt is advance-refunded through an irrevocable trust, the defeased debt is removed from the statement of net position. The $400,000 difference is reported as a deferred outflow of resources, amortized over the shorter of the remaining life of the old or new debt as an adjustment to interest expense.
Wrong (A): Both debts are not reported simultaneously -- legal defeasance removes the old debt from the statements.
