UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Under IFRS (IAS 2), reverse $450,000 of the write-down; under U.S. GAAP (ASC 330), no reversal is permitted","Both frameworks permit reversal of inventory write-downs up to the original $1,800,000 cost basis","Neither framework permits any reversal of inventory write-downs once the write-down has been recognized","Under U.S. GAAP, reverse the write-down to $1,650,000; under IFRS, the $1,200,000 remains permanent"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under IAS 2.33, inventory write-downs are reversed when NRV recovers, but only up to the original cost -- so Global reverses $450,000 ($1,650,000 minus $1,200,000). Under U.S. GAAP (ASC 330-10-35-1B), once inventory is written down, the reduced amount becomes the new cost basis and recoveries are not recognized.
Wrong (B): U.S. GAAP prohibits reversal of inventory write-downs; only IFRS permits reversal up to original cost.
