-- Q11540: Financial Reporting: For-Profit [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Machinery sales are revenue from central operations; the land profit is a gain from a peripheral transaction","Both items are revenue because they both increase net assets and result from exchange transactions","Both items are gains because they represent increases in equity from transactions with external parties","Machinery sales are gains and the land sale is revenue because gains require amounts exceeding $1,000,000"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under SFAC No. 8, Chapter 4, revenues arise from an entity''s ongoing major or central operations, while gains arise from peripheral or incidental transactions. Brookfield''s machinery sales are revenue because custom manufacturing is its core business; the land sale is a gain because selling real estate is incidental to its operations.
Wrong (B): Although both increase net assets, the Conceptual Framework distinguishes revenues from gains based on centrality of the activity.
Wrong (C): Machinery sales are revenue, not gains, because manufacturing is Brookfield''s primary business activity.
Wrong (D): There is no dollar threshold distinguishing revenue from gains; the classification depends on whether the activity is central or peripheral.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 11540;

