-- Q11662: Accounting Changes and Error Corrections [medium/L3]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Retrospectively restate all prior periods to remove equity method income previously recognized","Continue applying the equity method until the investment is ultimately sold or disposed of","Prospectively cease the equity method and carry the investment at its equity-method book value at the change date","Write the investment down to zero and recognize a loss for the full carrying amount"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 323-10-35-36 and ASC 250-10-45-17, when an investor loses significant influence due to dilution, it ceases applying the equity method prospectively. The investment retains its equity-method carrying amount at the change date and is subsequently accounted for under ASC 321.
